cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the original GSE164157 dataset."
title: "dpsc-wls-human-scRNAseq: WLS (GPR177/Wntless) expression in candidate human dental pulp stem cells"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Islam
    given-names: Md Tariqul
    affiliation: The ADA Forsyth Institute
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtariqi/dpsc-wls-human-scRNAseq"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R pipeline for a donor-aware single-cell RNA-seq analysis of
  WLS (GPR177/Wntless), the cargo receptor required for Wnt ligand secretion,
  in human dental pulp (GEO GSE164157; five donors, 10x Genomics). The
  workflow covers quality control, scDblFinder doublet removal, Harmony
  integration, marker-based cell type annotation, identification of candidate
  dental pulp stem cells, donor-paired pseudobulk edgeR tests, mixed-effects
  models and sensitivity analyses. Code is released under the MIT licence;
  reports, figures and tables under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - scRNA-seq
  - dental pulp stem cells
  - DPSC
  - WLS
  - Wntless
  - GPR177
  - Wnt signaling
  - Wnt secretion
  - pseudobulk
  - Harmony
  - Seurat
  - edgeR
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Single-cell RNA-seq of human dental pulp (GSE164157)"
    url: "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE164157"
    authors:
      - name: "Original GSE164157 submitters (see GEO record)"
    repository: "Gene Expression Omnibus"
